Round 80 (docs/ROUND80_PLAN.md A3, build/r80/hit/HIT_TRACE.md; the owner's
pick F-057, run on the standing OK F-059 (3)). Call 6 keeps the plan's
"70 (real 79)" with Grok's refinement (docs/collab/ROUND80_HELPERS_GROK.md):
at a shown 50 or less the game's number already is the real one, so no label.

Core: new zakuro-core fates_true_hit.rs. THRESHOLDS is our own table (the
2-roll average's threshold out of 10000 for each shown 0..100, from
build/r80/hit/true_hit_table.json), re-made in a test from the rule with a
true sine; no game bytes. shown_real(threshold): 100 only at 10000, 0 only at
0, else round(threshold / 100) clamped to 1..99. A label "real NN" is painted
only for a shown 51..99.

The forecast is found by reading only (never a trap, never a write): the three
proc list heads at 0x00752B48, the live proc with the target select's vtable
0x00635C5C, its BattleInfoWindow at +0x854 (+4 = BattleInfo, float +0x6C4 =
the slide-in; nothing is painted until it has slid in), the page from
GameConfigData *0x006DA0F8 +4 bit 7 (set = simple page), and each side's hit
at BattleInfo + k*0x200 + 0x30 (attack count +0x3C <= 0 = the dash, no label).
Detail page (the game's default): side 0's label right of its "%", side 1's
left of its number, each painted only when a light/dark check sees that
side's single-column Hit row (an Attack Stance pair's two columns get no
label in this first version). Simple page: places from the draw code, outside
each number. Glyphs are the growth view's 5x7 table (fates_growth_view::glyph,
now pub(crate)), cream on brown, one native pixel per dot.

Hook: System::read_scaled paints into its own copy of the top picture
(true_hit_paint), and the frontend's shown / shown_right take the top screen
from that picture instead of straight from the GPU while true_hit_shown() is
true, as the growth view does for the bottom screen.

Defaults are today's game: with True hit Off (or no [fates_helpers] table)
helpers().true_hit() is checked first, nothing is read and the picture and
the GPU path are exactly as before. True hit only paints the host's copy of
the screen; guest memory is never written.

